WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.140
A sticky note on a desk.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.370
Three words: sleep in Macbeth.

3
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.620
It grows into a cloud of
everything you could say.

4
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:12.020
A scroll unrolls, right
off the edge of the screen.

5
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.900
The play gives you plenty.

6
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.020
Just after the murder,
Macbeth hears a voice cry,

7
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.860
"Sleep no more!"

8
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.150
So is that sticky note
a line of inquiry yet?

9
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.720
Or something else?

10
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:26.700
In this mission, you'll meet the HL essay:

11
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:32.360
1,200 to 1,500 words, built
round your own line of inquiry.

12
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:37.460
You'll test whether a longer, more detailed
topic is any closer to a line of inquiry.

13
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.870
And you'll squeeze the
topic through a funnel,

14
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.490
one stage at a time.

15
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.970
Your mission: explain the difference
between a topic and a line of inquiry.
